A||N||2||Taijiguy||I SMELL SMOKE!!!||||10||
Z||000000||Taijiguy||08-07-2000||10:21 AM||||Well, for those of you who have been following the saga; I started the beast last night (This morning actually-at about 2 a.m.) That motor with that cam, minus the fuel injection system, ROMPS! It has a lope to it I never had with the injection stuff, and it just SOUNDS like it has more torque. It's amazing the difference without the injection stuff. The exhaust system is the same as before, but the sound is much more resonant, and throatier. I need to adjust the accelerator pump, but it seems the response wil be extremely crisp. It just sounds MEAN. Can't wait to get the details worked out and take 'er for a SPIN!!  YEEEEEEHaaaaaw!<P>-Taiji<P>(...is one happy mo-fo)||||reg||10
Z||000001||My7Fieros||08-07-2000||04:46 PM||||PHEW! Man, I thought I was going to hear yet ANOTHER "Fiero fire" story! Don't scare me like that! <BR>Glad to hear she's running good! Keep us posted!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Taijiguy||08-08-2000||02:09 AM||||Ooooh, yeah. I fergot about that. Heheee...didn't mean to throw a scare into anyone! <BR>Well, the saga continues. I just got home (2 a.m. again) I was finishing the engine compartment wiring, got that pretty much wrapped up. I couldn't wait to get to the car today, since it was so late last night, and I couldn't really fire it up and let it romp. First thing I did was track down a tapping noise, and found a valve I either missed, or loosened up on me a bit. Adjusted that sucker (fortunately it was on the REAR bank, for benefit of reemoving the valve cover) Fired it up, and it ran like a charm. The idle is SOOOOOO lopey, pop the throttle, and it jumps to attention, and mean RIGHT NOW! This mother is gonna ROCK! I love it! I will need to rejet the carb and adjust the accelerator pump down some, since it's running a bit rich. Also still need to hook up the electric choke and a few other details. But for the most part, it's ready to hit the road. Well, except for the fact that the body is all in pieces, which is a whole 'NOTHER story, as we progress into the paint portion of the buildup. Stay tuned.<P>-Taiji||||reg||1
